## Open Issues Requiring Cycle 4+

1. **C9 structural fix**: re-baseline to Day 365 board readiness; SOC 2 Type II observation window starts Day 60
2. **C1**: lock Big 4 audit partner BEFORE Series A close to convert PCAOB claim from assertion to certified barrier
3. **C2**: rebase base-case waste to 14% (not 18%); change headline to "9–19x ROI range depending on maturity tier"
4. **C5**: introduce reference-customer gate; revise sales-cycle estimate to 12–18 months; revise CAC to $800K–$1.5M all-in
5. **C6**: split Moat 1 into Federal/Defense track (FedRAMP Mod + CMMC) and FSI track (FFIEC + NYDFS + SOC 2); replace synthetic cold-start with design-partner data-seeding program
6. **C7**: add CPA-reviewer retainer; reframe "PCAOB-defensible" → "PCAOB AS 2201-aligned control evidence package"
7. **C8**: add Risk #20 FedRAMP Moderate authorization delay; downgrade Lloyd's syndicate to excess-layer; add 2-of-3 multi-model consensus gate

## Final Recommendation

**Not board-ready. Path to board readiness clear.** Run Cycle 4 against Thesis v4 (incorporates all 7 open issues above). Strategy is materially sharper than v1; remaining gaps are about execution timeline math and partnership lock-ins, not strategic positioning.

Run cost (3 cycles, 10 parallel Sonnet agents per cycle): ~870K tokens total across 30 agent invocations.
